{{Quote|The Clone Wars era is probably my favorite in all of Star Wars. It has it all &mdash; big adventure, sweeping romance, Force mythology, Jedi powers, and, of course, the awesome clones. This event series is going to bring together all the best, evergreen parts of ''Star Wars'' and weave a story that longtime fans (like myself) and new, younger readers (like my own kids) will definitely love.|Michael Moreci|<ref name="Announcement" />}}
'''''Star Wars Adventures: The Clone Wars – Battle Tales''''' is a five-issue [[canon]] [[Star Wars comic books|comic]] miniseries published by [[IDW Publishing]]. Written by [[Michael Moreci]], the series is set during the [[Clone Wars]], focusing on characters from the animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''. The [[Star Wars Adventures: The Clone Wars – Battle Tales 1|first issue]] of the series was set to be published on [[April 1]], [[2020]],<ref name="Announcement" /> but it was pushed back due to the [[Wikipedia:Coronavirus disease 2019|COVID-19]] [[Wikipedia:2019–20 coronavirus pandemic|pandemic]].<ref name="CBR">{{WebCite|url=https://www.cbr.com/idw-publishing-suspends-comics-diamond-distributors-coronavirus-covid19|text=IDW Suspends May Releases, Reduces Publishing Line Due to Diamond Hiatus|work=CBR|archivedate=20200324150614}}</ref> The first issue was eventually resolicited for [[June 3]], [[2020]],<ref name="Comixology">{{Comixology|url=Star-Wars-Adventures-Clone-Wars-1-of-5/digital-comic/838766|text=Star Wars Adventures: Clone Wars #1 (of 5)}}</ref> though it was later moved to [[May 20]].<ref name="Amazon1" />

Set early in ''The Clone Wars'' television series, ''Battle Tales'' centers on a group of [[clone trooper]]s sharing stories about the war, similar to [[Cavan Scott]]'s ''[[Star Wars Adventures: Tales from Vader's Castle]]''. However, the stories told by the [[Cloning|clones]] in ''Battle Tales'' are not like the more tall-tale-leaning stories seen in ''Tales from Vader's Castle''. Moreci felt that the clones were not the type of characters to share tall tales. During the development of the comic, Moreci tried to have [[Gregor|CC-5576-39]] "Gregor" appear, but this was denied.<ref name="Moreci Interview">{{YouTube|video=Dy_yNQXhfUw|text=Why You Should Be Excited for The Clone Wars: Battle Tales - Interview with Writer Michael Moreci|channel=@StarWarsExplained|name=Star Wars Explained}}</ref>
